        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "93395834-4169-5817-983b-c44096225c84",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Australian Young Labor, Australian Labor Party, Australian Parliament, Australian Workers Union\n- People: Tony Burke, Bob Carr, John Faulkner, Bill Shorten\n- Roles: youth wing, president, NSW Premier, Federal Minister for Agriculture, Special Minister of State, House of Representatives member, Manager of Opposition Business, Shadow Minister\n\nFacts:\n- Australian Young Labor is the youth wing of the Australian Labor Party and represents Australian Labor Party members aged 14 to 26.\n- Former presidents of Australian Young Labor have included Bob Carr, Tony Burke, John Faulkner, and Bill Shorten.\n- Bob Carr is a former NSW Premier.\n- Tony Burke was a Federal Minister for Agriculture.\n- John Faulkner was a Special Minister of State and a senator.\n- Bill Shorten was the national secretary of the Australian Workers Union and later became the member for Maribyrnong and Federal Labor Leader.\n- Anthony Stephen Burke was born on 4 November 1969.\n- Tony Burke is a Labor member of the House of Representatives in the Australian Parliament for Watson, New South Wales.\n- Tony Burke has served as Manager of Opposition Business and as Shadow Minister for the Arts, for Environment and Water, and for Citizenship and Multicultural Australia.",
